-- #1618 — a SINGLE impl whose head carries an effect row, `<Stdout> Int`.
--
-- There is no overlap here to be rejected for, and nothing about this program is
-- ambiguous: one interface, one impl, one call. It CHECKS clean (exit 0) and RUNS
-- correctly (`medaka run` prints 2), and then it CANNOT BE BUILT — `medaka build`
-- exits 1 with a compiler E-PANIC, one effect row away from a program that builds
-- and runs fine (control.mdk).
--
-- HAND-DERIVED CORRECT ANSWER: the only impl of `Sz` whose head matches the
-- receiver is this one, so `sz 0` is its body, 2 — which is exactly what `medaka
-- run` already prints. The defect is NOT the value; it is that the emitter cannot
-- find the impl the front end already resolved. Correct behaviour is therefore
-- `medaka build` exiting 0 and the binary printing 2, like control.mdk does.
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int

impl Sz (<Stdout> Int) where
  sz _ = 2

main = println (sz 0)
